\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Lord Jesus, in the days of old
\par Two walked with Thee in waning light;
\par And love's blind instinct made them bold
\par To crave Thy presence through the night.
\par As night descends, we too would pray:
\par O leave us not at close of day!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Did not their hearts within them burn?
\par And though their Lord they failed to know,
\par Did not their spirits inly yearn?
\par They  could not let the Stranger go.
\par Much more must we who know Thee pray:
\par O leave us not at close of day!
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Perchance we have not always wist
\par Who has been with us by the way;
\par Amid day's uproar we have missed
\par Some word that Thou hast had to say.
\par In silent night, O Saviour dear,
\par We would not fail Thy voice to hear.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Day is far spent, and night is nigh;
\par Stay with us, Saviour, through the night;
\par Talk with us, touch us tenderly
\par Lead us to peace, to rest, to light;
\par Dispel our darkness with Thy face,
\par Radiant with resurrection grace.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Nor this night only, blessed Lord,
\par We, every day and every hour,
\par Would walk with Thee Emmaus-ward
\par To hear Thy voice of love and power;
\par And every night would by Thy side
\par Look, listen, and be satisfied.
\par \f1 
